{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered","id":90113,"title":"Will issues of resourse depletion and sustainability and global warming be covered?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-13T05:03:17-07:00","id":90113,"title":"Will issues of resourse depletion and sustainability and global warming be covered?","content":"One thing I loved about the original Trinity was how it covered various ideologies of the future eg The Joyceans and provided various backgrounds, environments and organisations that reflected those ideologies.<br /> <br /> I hope that this will be expanded upon and updated to include Peak Oil, Global weirding (warming), sustainability, pollution, currency wars, class wars, bank coups, the globally linked economy etc and how the setting and people are affected by these issues. Or the consequences of ignoring them and continuing to follow an economic model that demands constant growth in a finite world of diminishing resources and greater population and greater energy demands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2501-jae","name":"Jae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T05:36:01-07:00","id":90146,"title":"","content":"*sadly puts away mechanics for gasoline-powered mecha*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T07:05:05-07:00","id":90179,"title":"","content":"Neall don't you dare","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:55:59-07:00","id":90251,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, by the time of Trinity, fossil fuels were largely a relic of the past. They had largely been replaced by cheap and efficient electric fuel cells. They ability to have portable, reliable power has also helped decentralize a good portion of the population. At least from the material, many social ills have persisted, but at least conflict over energy seem largely solved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T11:20:47-07:00","id":90348,"title":"","content":"Don't worry, guys, we're replacing gasoline-powered mecha with mecha powered by baby seals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T12:15:47-07:00","id":90374,"title":"","content":"I..... I actually want to play that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T13:21:39-07:00","id":90399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered#post90113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I loved about the original Trinity was how it covered various ideologies of the future eg The Joyceans and provided various backgrounds, environments and organisations that reflected those ideologies.<br /> <br /> I hope that this will be expanded upon and updated to include Peak Oil, Global weirding (warming), sustainability, pollution, currency wars, class wars, bank coups, the globally linked economy etc and how the setting and people are affected by these issues. Or the consequences of ignoring them and continuing to follow an economic model that demands constant growth in a finite world of diminishing resources and greater population and greater energy demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling that the actions of all the crazy, ungodly potent superpeople during the Aberrant War will still have a greater weight than those other things. One of them accidentally sunk Florida. Maybe another one triggered Peak Oil by turning the oil back into dinosaurs that were hungry for human flesh..<br /> <br /> Also, if I'm going to use a mecha, I want one powered the old-fashioned way, with steam.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2013/137/8/4/robot_lincoln_by_johntfs-d65kl4o.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 03-13-2014, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T14:46:19-07:00","id":90427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=90348#post90348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, guys, we're replacing gasoline-powered mecha with mecha powered by baby seals.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all the global warming, pollution and habitat loss, I fear we may rapidly reach Peak Seal\u00ae. I just bet Aberrant science is on the verge of orphan powered mecha - we can meet our energy needs while fighting overpopulation.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, the effects of advanced Aberrant science and the Aberrant War, together with vast resources and space available from Lunar, Martian and orbital colonies in the Trinity Era, render our current political and sociological issues largely irrelevant. Although both Trinity and Aberrant were reflections of 1990's (as were the other WW properties), I hope and expect an updated and more mature feel to a&quot;reimagined&quot; or updated Aeonverse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T16:43:02-07:00","id":90494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=90427#post90427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With all the global warming, pollution and habitat loss, I fear we may rapidly reach Peak Seal\u00ae. I just bet Aberrant science is on the verge of orphan powered mecha - we can meet our energy needs while fighting overpopulation.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, the effects of advanced Aberrant science and the Aberrant War, together with vast resources and space available from Lunar, Martian and orbital colonies in the Trinity Era, render our current political and sociological issues largely irrelevant. Although both Trinity and Aberrant were reflections of 1990's (as were the other WW properties), I hope and expect an updated and more mature feel to a&quot;reimagined&quot; or updated Aeonverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>But who doesn't love the 90s?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://cdn0.dailydot.com/uploaded/images/original/2013/3/4/Screen_Shot_2013-03-04_at_4.16.15_PM.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T17:23:07-07:00","id":90516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=90494#post90494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But who doesn't love the 90s?</div> </div> </div> </div>So very true. However, I'm a child of the 1980's and have seen too much change, for good and ill. My identity and education involved the Cold War, global cooling and fears of the next ice age, and the swoosh, swoosh of my parachute pants as I strutted through the hallowed halls of junior high. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://img1.etsystatic.com/002/0/6230905/il_570xN.352952363_bg37.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T04:32:41-07:00","id":90790,"title":"","content":"Given that the Trinity setting includes asteriod mining, advanced biotech, and multiple new ways of generating power, which reasources are limited would be changed. But then people in 1880's London worried about how the 21st century would clear away all the horse dung. We'll have plenty of problems in the 22nd century, but the ones we'll focus ones will probably be brand new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T13:29:34-07:00","id":91053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered#post90113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I loved about the original Trinity was how it covered various ideologies of the future eg The Joyceans and provided various backgrounds, environments and organisations that reflected those ideologies.<br /> <br /> I hope that this will be expanded upon and updated to include Peak Oil, Global weirding (warming), sustainability, pollution, currency wars, class wars, bank coups, the globally linked economy etc and how the setting and people are affected by these issues. Or the consequences of ignoring them and continuing to follow an economic model that demands constant growth in a finite world of diminishing resources and greater population and greater energy demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>They already deal with a lot of those things in the first edition, some up front and others implied by things like the tech and society.<br /> <br /> Peak Oil is not a big issue when most vehicles are powered by batteries charged from the mains, fuel cells, bio processes of some kind, biofuels, solar, or even nuclear power. The Esperenza disaster documentation mentions that the ubiquitous and normally clean and safe microfusion generators that power much of the world mysteriously exploded near the impact points, so things like coal and oil fired power plants were probably gone long before. The microfusion process was becoming commercially viable in the \u201cnow\u201d of the game so it is probably safe to assume that fossil fuel use was mostly gone by about 2020 with the mania with which Nova-tech was embraced by society at the time.<br /> <br /> Global warming might still be an issue in Trinity, I do not remember anything specific about it in the fluff offhand, but whatever greenhouse gasses hardtech would still produce would probably be offset by the biotech absorbing them for its own use. The loss of huge tracts of vegetation in North America and possibly in Europe to taint effects, and loss of rain forest to clearing for farms elsewhere could pose some problems but it is probably offset by things like the greening of Ethiopia and growing use of biotech (there is even mention of some self-sustaining biotech arcologies in one of the books).<br /> <br /> Sustainability is probably still something of an issue but not a particularly pressing one since energy is not a big problem by then and there are a lot more options for recycling than there are today, including an extensive array of biotech ones like digestive materials separation/sorting and whatnot. In addition, there are asteroid and extraterrestrial planet based mines bringing in new resources as well. Terra is in much the same position as the industrialized early USA east coast, with a vast wilderness to explore and exploit available.<br /> <br /> Pollution and Politics (including economics) seem to be the biggest issues on that list that would still be a problem. Besides chemical toxins there is the issue of radiation (particularly in Shattered Europe) and Taint, and the Orders killed off their best experts in the radiation and taint departments so they are stuck with the problems until they can develop some other way to handle them. Mostly they seem to cover up the problem in the fluff.<br /> <br /> On the political and economic fronts it seems to be business as usual, the main difference being the players are all shuffled around and todays third world are the leaders in the future and the big players of today have sunk considerably (which is chillingly realistic if the current trend continues).<br /> <br /> Some of the colony writeups mention population pressure, political differences and/or power games, profit, and even just general wanderlust and scientific curiosity as reasons for various colonies being started so those factors obviously still exist too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T11:46:06-07:00","id":92906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=90399#post90399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the feeling that the actions of all the crazy, ungodly potent superpeople during the Aberrant War will still have a greater weight than those other things. One of them accidentally sunk Florida. Maybe another one triggered Peak Oil by turning the oil back into dinosaurs that were hungry for human flesh..</div> </div> </div> </div>Dinosaurs didn't turn into oil deposits. They turned into uranium deposits. There are some specimens of diplodocids formerly known as <i>Seismosaurus</i> that had absorbed so much uranium over their time sitting in the western US sediments that they would fluoresce under a UV lamp, which made them rather easy to find at night,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-18-2014, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T14:20:14-07:00","id":93794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=92906#post92906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dinosaurs didn't turn into oil deposits. They turned into uranium deposits. There are some speciments of diplodocids formerly known as Seismosaurus that had absorbed so much uranium over their time sitting in the western US sediments that they would fluoresce under a UV lamp, which made them rather easy to find at night,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem with Ascending... always leaving dem valuable Sariras behind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T21:29:01-07:00","id":124983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=90348#post90348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, guys, we're replacing gasoline-powered mecha with mecha powered by baby seals.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=326OpacxyMI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=326OpacxyMI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=326OpacxyMI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=326OpacxyMI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:35:56-07:00","id":163901,"title":"","content":"It would really just take 1 aberrant with the power to convert CO2 into anything else, or just one SMART!(tm) abby to make a supersciency atmospheric carbon reducer!(tm) to solve our &quot;problems&quot; but frankly, why SOLVE a problem in a story when you can make it worse! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Frankly it seemed to me by the time of Trinity that you could have WAY more interesting conflicts considering your average joe could afford a low power fusion rocket and strap that to a rock you'd end up with people having the power to change the orbits of some nasty rocks. And considering what happened with the Esperanza I'd figure the big &quot;problem&quot; of the Trinity Era would be Orbit Control.<br /> I am even right now playing it up as a background political element in my current game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:33:46-07:00","id":166012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Galaxy Master Zhad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=163901#post163901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would really just take 1 aberrant with the power to convert CO2 into anything else, or just one SMART!(tm) abby to make a supersciency atmospheric carbon reducer!(tm) to solve our &quot;problems&quot; but frankly, why SOLVE a problem in a story when you can make it worse! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Antaeus for two-in-one! Being a plant-man pays off in the carbon-based economy. (^VVVVVV^)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T17:04:05-07:00","id":166359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Galaxy Master Zhad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=163901#post163901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would really just take 1 aberrant with the power to convert CO2 into anything else, or just one SMART!(tm) abby to make a supersciency atmospheric carbon reducer!(tm) to solve our &quot;problems&quot; but frankly, why SOLVE a problem in a story when you can make it worse!</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually a big part of the Aberrant and Trinity games, wasn't it? They solved pretty much <i>all</i> those problems in the Nova Age, but when the novas and aberrants left Earth in 2061, a lot of those supersciency things (and the changes created by direct application of nova powers) slowly faded -- without novas around to maintain them, things fell apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:18:35-07:00","id":166981,"title":"","content":"Oh really? I haven't played trinity and I understand that after such a devastating conflict some knowledge would be lost but did they lost all their technological development? how is that possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:45:30-07:00","id":167000,"title":"","content":"A combination of a few things.<br /> <br /> 1. At the conclusion of the Aberrant War, there were two novas who spent a great deal of their time within the OpNet, existing as energy signals &quot;riding the rails&quot;, so to speak. One of them was a Terat named Synapse, who was very anti-baseline but was also relatively sane due to Chrysalis. The other was Mungu Kuwasha, now known as &quot;Backlash&quot;, who had started out pro-baseline but gradually went insane over the decades due to Taint. Backlash ambushed Synapse, and the two of them fought for hours across the OpNet. Eventually, Synapse won -- but Backlash's &quot;death scream&quot; was essentially a quantum-powered EMP that blasted throughout the OpNet and shorted out most, if not all, technological devices connected to it. All electronic information that wasn't in air-gapped servers or printed in hard copy file cabinets was lost. This includes a significant amount of technological know-how.<br /> <br /> 2. Many inventions created by novas are what are termed &quot;Advancements&quot; in the game system. Advancements are a form of technology based on mundane, legitimate scientific knowledge -- they're very advanced, though, so they're much better than anything anyone else is doing. An advancement is anything that a baseline <i>could</i> theoretically make allowed by the Laws of Nature. The OpNet, synthetic eufiber, the hyper-combustion engine, and flying cars are all examples of advancements. <i>HOWEVER</i>, there is another type of invention that novas can create. These are termed &quot;Innovations&quot;. Innovations are devices which are <i>not</i> based on scientific principles -- they are created as an extension of a nova's world-changing Quantum powers. Essentially, these Innovations are just devices that somehow recreate a Quantum power. Because <i>only</i> novas can channel and properly control Quantum, an Innovation requires a nova operator (or at least, a nova technician to make sure it stays in working order). When the novas and aberrants left after the Ultimatum, there was no one on Earth who could maintain any of the incredibly advanced devices. Example Innovations would include climate-control devices, global CO2 scrubbers, terraforming equipment, interstellar spacecraft, RNA sequences that let infected individuals adapt to any environment, a Cerebro-like device, etc.<br /> <br /> Combined, this means that when the novas left, they took their understanding of their Innovations with them. And when the OpNet failed, Earth lost most (but not <i>all</i>) of its understanding of the Advancements made during the Nova Age, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:49:25-07:00","id":167004,"title":"","content":"A few ways -<br /> <br /> Many of the environmental fixes were the result of nova powers or nova technology. Many of the more radical nova Tech inventions operated using the same &quot;breaking the laws of physics&quot; principles the novas themselves employed. Without a Nova to maintain it, much of the Nova Tech simply ceased to function.<br /> <br /> The Aberrant War was devastating. Some of the more powerful Nova's were natural disasters on legs. The result of these forces in conflict crippled large portions of the existing infrastructure. Most notably, a clash between two cyber-kinetics destroyed the op -net (like the internet, but better), permanently erasing a vast amount of information stored on servers with online access.<br /> <br /> As a result, many of the post-war factions were very leery of anything that seemed Aberrant-like, probably including a fair amount on non-Nova advancements.<br /> All in all, for a few decades the world went into a mini - dark age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:01:26-07:00","id":167018,"title":"","content":"Until Operation Rewrite came along! Bless Project Utopia!<br /> <br /> Man, I hate them... Mercer probably had a conniption when he found out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:54:26-07:00","id":167075,"title":"","content":"Operation rewrite? Chrysalis? To the wiki!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:17:36-07:00","id":167095,"title":"","content":"Chrysalis is a means by which members of the Teragen could manage their Taint -- essentially letting them guide and direct their own &quot;evolution&quot; instead of just letting it happen. The most prominent and favorable feature of Chrysalis was the ability to take <i>mental</i> aberrations and turn them into <i>physical</i> aberrations -- it could not forestall your distancing from baseline humanity, but it <i>could</i> keep you completely sane and of sound mental state. The best explanation I've heard is that Taint turns you into an insane human monster, while Chrysalis turns you into a sane <i>in</i>human monster.<br /> <br /> Project Rewrite (sorry, I got the name wrong the first time) was an effort by the Aeon Society to &quot;fix&quot; the damage wrought by the destruction of the OpNet. With the loss of so much information, Aeon tried to collate all of the remaining knowledge it could -- be it from computers that were thankfully disconnected from the OpNet at the time, or hard copies left in boxes in someone's basement. They did not, however, just re-upload all of this information: they went through and selectively chose what to allow back into the world. Information that they deemed &quot;dangerous&quot; or in opposition to their world-view was suppressed and removed. They pretty much used the whole thing as a way to completely and totally revise history to their preferences. In this way, successive generations gradually forgot about the mistakes Project Utopia (and, by extension, the Aeon Society) made with novas. Big things like that weren't exactly <i>forgotten</i> in their entirety, but they <i>were</i> put in a different light. For example, the loss of the OpNet: while it was actually a result of two novas fighting each other, that idea didn't fit the concept of turning novas and aberrants into a monolithic opposition force (why would two guys on the same &quot;side&quot; try so hard to kill each other?). Instead, they simply removed Synapse from most records. In the version of history most people in the Trinity Era know, Backlash destroyed the OpNet &quot;just to see if he could&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T13:41:53-07:00","id":167200,"title":"","content":"What a bunch of opportunistic a&amp;$%holes. I have only read adventure, how did the incredibly cool and idealistic aeon society turned into shield and then into hydra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T13:51:33-07:00","id":167208,"title":"","content":"Mercer vanished. Without his driving light and humanitarian values, Aeon slowly started falling apart. There's a journal entry by Whitley Styles in Aberrant, lamenting how the higher-ups in Aeon are slowly losing their sense of enlightened morality while simultaneously convincing themselves that everything they're doing is &quot;for the greater good&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T03:03:01-07:00","id":167707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=90348#post90348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, guys, we're replacing gasoline-powered mecha with mecha powered by baby seals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do hope they were clubbed to death, Ian. Otherwise this will be a no go for me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T07:50:03-07:00","id":167910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=167707#post167707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do hope they were clubbed to death, Ian. Otherwise this will be a no go for me...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iElGoLQSlGE\" data-code=\"iElGoLQSlGE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iElGoLQSlGE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:02:26-07:00","id":170145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/90113-will-issues-of-resourse-depletion-and-sustainability-and-global-warming-be-covered?p=167910#post167910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iElGoLQSlGE\" data-code=\"iElGoLQSlGE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iElGoLQSlGE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Brilliant!<br /> <br /> I am also totally cool with all the COOL TECH! (tm) having been taken with the abbys when they &quot;left&quot; earth. Though I do think some of the normal stuff they made, like fusion power and such were saved. Also I did like the damage done to the earth by the Trinity Era. Basically all the good done was reversed but rather then Global Climate Catastrophe you have more localized disasters. Like the Heartlands of North-America being a proper wasteland, Australia experiencing a population boom, Europe and the Middle East going through a new dark age, etc.<br /> <br /> On a tech front I personally just nipped the Artificial Gravity in the butt, that is just a personal thing, most folks wouldn't bother but I lean a bit towards more Hard Sci-fi with generic Tech. And Artificial Gravity (not psuedo gravity) is just asking for blackhole weapons and relativistic weapons to happen. Also they allow for forcefields. Think about it and you'll figure out way. Or just watch some clips from Space Engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:58:04-08:00","id":332509,"title":"","content":"Hello all, thank you for keeping this inspired setting alive. (pun intended) I legitimately got goosebumps and butterflies in my stomach when i saw there were actual publishers interested in continuing the setting.<br /> <br /> I did find myself often wondering how i could disable the Zushima Macrobe created by Dr &quot;Antaeus&quot; Balmer, as i agree with Zhad above, that an ecologically bankrupted earth yields a few new possibilities the utopian 'magic macrobe' perspective doesn't lend itself to. The ideas sometimes dropped by futurists for limited terraforming of the earth to allow further exploitation are just too heart-breaking to pass up on (e.g. stained white magnesium skies), just the kind of arrogance that fits in with the setting in my opinion.<br /> Some of the climate change would even open up certain areas of the world for story development - the thawing arctic ocean and terraformed reserviors in the UAN (and other newly developed states) to bleed off increased sea levels in vast new maritime environs could make for interesting boom towns and even nations considering the scale. A thriving economy and ecology in what was once unused desert or plains could help mitigate some of the lost hope from the fall of the mother earth. The setting i love walked that fine line between utopia and dystopia, but as time passed this topic started to stick out like a sore thumb - although easily fixed.<br /> <br /> As mentioned above; I had always assumed that certain bits of super-science found in the original Trinity setting were dubious Nova inventions (Innovations) that became too useful too mothball or simply impossible to stop, like the macrobe. Psuedo gravity stuck out the most here - Zhad's logic directly above my post (To paraphrase; Where are the derivative weapons and other gravitational tech?) is the reason i assumed the post-utopia society locked away technological advances that were poorly understood. That some of these technologies slipped through the loophole was necessitated by the Rewrite project or other goals championed by the Trinity organization (generation arks, terraforming, etc...)<br /> I assumed hyper-fusion birlesme chambers were also in this category and Banji monopolized the industry from the (admittedly unpublished) Nihonjin remnants described in the web supplement &quot;Asia Ascendant&quot; or whatever it was called...<br /> In any case, the ecological strain on earth isn't the only planetary concern in the setting (especially after 2121 and the return of the Upeo and renewal of extrasolar exploration/settlement) and while certain pockets of ecological balance clearly exist in the original source material (Sudamerica stands out) - the ruined, depleted earth is a powerful motivator for expansion into the solar system and beyond. We already have the world in tatters after 2061 and earth's resources and sustainability should be easy enough to slip in. It would go a long way to adressing the (impressively few) scientific discrepancies between the original setting and a more modern understanding. The pockets of balance could be realistically maintained with industrious effort where needed, using biotech and theoretically sound hard-tech solutions in concert.<br /> I personally consider the setting's (mostly) hard science a strength - anything outside of our current framework is given a decent reason for being there. (e.g. Nova Innovations, Inspired Objects/Locations, Godlike Doyen/Aberrants) Why, i'd even see sense in a kind of suspended-reality for a period after (and even before) the Hammersmith effect and Process 418, not unlike the different galactic zones in Vernor Vinge's &quot;A Fire in the Sky&quot;.<br /> So i hope the new books take a few lines to deal with this - after-all it really doesn't require much work.<br /> Thanks for reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":". 12-07-2014, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}